#napoveda_koren
<FONT=latin216.fv>Bloüek<SF> - text editor and image viewer

Help topics:
1) <OK="napoveda_klavesy">Keyboard control<OK/>
2) <OK="napoveda_mys">Mouse control<OK/>
3) <OK="napoveda_prvky">Control elements<OK/>

#napoveda_klavesy
<FONT=surea37.fn;barva=65346>Keyboard control<SB;SF>
<barva=65535>F10<sb>   - enter main menu
<barva=65535>F1<sb>    - make a new file
<barva=65535>F2<sb>    - save file
<barva=65535>F3<sb>    - load file
<barva=65535>Alt+F3<sb> - close file
<barva=65535>Alt+F1<sb> - load this file (INFO.TXT)
<barva=65535>Ctrl+F<sb> - search
<barva=65535>Ctrl+S<sb> - search again
<barva=65535>Ctrl+H<sb> - replace
<barva=65535>Ctrl+A<sb> - select all document to block
<barva=65535>Ctrl+Q<sb> - offers a variant for last written character (like a-†-•-...])
<barva=65535>Ctrl+K<sb> - char conversion functions
<barva=65535>Ctrl+L<sb> - quick call for line adjustement functions
<barva=65535>LShift+Alt<sb> - change keyboard layout
<barva=65535>Ctrl+Alt+Up<sb> - select actual line to block
<barva=65535>Ctrl+Alt+Down<sb> - word on the cursor to block
<barva=65535>Ctrl+Alt+Left<sb> - all characters from cursor to left to block
<barva=65535>Ctrl+Alt+Right<sb> - all characters from cursor to right to block
<barva=65535>Backspace<sb> - delete one character left to cursor
<barva=65535>Delete<sb> - delete one character right to cursor
<barva=65535>Shift+Delete<sb> - delete selected block
<barva=65535>*arrows<sb> - cursor movements
<barva=65535>*Ctrl+PageUp<sb> or <barva=65535>*Ctrl+Home<sb> - jumps on first line of the file
<barva=65535>*Ctrl+PageDown<sb> or <barva=65535>*Ctrl+End<sb>- jumps on last line of the file
<barva=65535>*Ctrl+RightArrow<sb> - moves one word to right
<barva=65535>*Ctrl+LeftArrow<sb> - moves one word to left
   These function keys (marked with the "*" char) can be combined with the <Shift> key.
   In such case is together *with cursor movement also created or updated the text
   selection block.
<barva=65535>Ctrl+[1-7]<sb> - copy selected block of text into clipboard No 1-7
<barva=65535>Alt+[1-7]<sb> - paste text from clipboard No 1-7 into cursor position
<barva=65535>Ctrl+plus<sb> and <barva=65535>Ctrl+minus<sb> (on the numeric keyboard) - fast switching among opened files forward or backward
<barva=65535>ESC<sb>   - quit
<barva=65535>Alt+F2<sb> - make a screenshot

#napoveda_mys
<FONT=surea37.fn;barva=65346>Mouse control<SB;SF>
<barva=65535>1) In document window<SB>
Left mouse button (LMB) click  - move cursor to selected text place
LMB click+shift - select beginning and end of the text block
LMB press and drag - interactive selection of the text block
Right mouse (RMB) click - shows information and optionally a conversion menu for the char you clicked to.
Also accesses functions for work with bookmarks.

<barva=65535>2) In panel with cards of opened files<SB>
LMB click - switches the main window to the specified file
RMB click - several actions with the specified file
(close, close all but this, show full file path)

<barva=65535>3) In the clipboards indicators<SB>
LMB click - menu for operations with the clipboard

<barva=65535>4) Other notes<SB>
->> All other buttons and other GUI elements use only left mouse button at this moment.
    The right one is not used currently.
->> Nearly all dialog boxes can be moved by dragging their title bar.
->> Dragging text with left mouse button over information windows like this one can select text blocks to 
    copy to clipboard with Ctrl+[1-7] to pasting to document window.

#napoveda_prvky
<FONT=surea37.fn;barva=65346>Control elements<SB;SF>
Most of the workplace is covered by the <barva=65535>main window<SB>. In this window, it displays either a document with editable text or viewer with loaded image. 
Along the left side of the editor window, there's an optional panel with indicators showing where the individual lines in the document are terminated.
Above the editor or viewer are three horizontal panels.

<barva=65535>1) Permanent panel<SB>
The main menu with items: <barva=65535>File<SB>, <barva=65535>Text<SB>, <barva=65535>Options<SB>, <barva=65535>Help<SB>
To right from this menu are the <OK="napoveda_indikatory">clipboard indicators<OK/> for the text blocks numbered 1-7.
Even more to right (in the upper right corner) is a dropdown list where the keyboard layout can be selected.
This list can also be opened by pressing <OK="napoveda_klavesy">ALT+SHIFT<OK/>

<barva=65535>2) Context panel<SB>
It changes the main window content accordingly.
If an image is currently viewed, the left side shows their dimensions in pixels. To right from this are buttons for fullscreen, for optimal window size and for rotating and flipping the image.
If an editable document is viewed, the context panel is different. On the left side is a button linking to the code page conversion functions dialog (can also be activated by pressing <OK="napoveda_klavesy">CTRL+K<OK/>).
On the right side, there's a button to change word wrapping options.
On the right from this button is a checkbox which switches the wrapping and non-wrapping mode. Along the right border, the current cursor position is displayed.

<barva=65535>3) Panel with cards of opened files<SB>
Until no file is loaded the third panel is empty. When some file is opened, its card is displayed in this panel. In the
<FONT=latin216.fv>Bloüek<SF> editor, it is possible to have simultaneously opened many files.
Their cards are displayed next to next and user can switch among them by the <OK="napoveda_mys">mouse.<OK/>.
The left mouse button switches the main window to specified file (document or image). The right mouse button opens a submenu allowing the closing the file, closing all files but this and the function for displaying the full path to the file.

#napoveda_indikatory
If some text is copied to clipboard by pressing <OK="napoveda_klavesy">CTRL+[1-7]<OK/> or a special button in some dialog windows, the presence of the content in a particular clipboard is indicated.
The indicator goes white and resembles a lit light bulb.
If a clipboard is empty, it displays in black and with symbol of a overstriked circle.
Indicator of clipboard No.7 can be displayed as <BARVA=65535>7W<SB>. This means that MS Windows clipboard services (or a compatible interface) are available. In this case, clipboard No.7 is linked to the Windows clipboard and it is possible to exchange blocks of text with other programs. Details in the TECHNOTE.TXT file.

#text_napovedy
<FONT=surea37.fn>Bloüek<SF>
<FONT=latin216.fv>version 1.76
Date of compilation: <BARVA=65535>30.3.2025<SB>
programmed by Laaca (laaca@seznam.cz)

Bloüek is text editor and image viewer which is
capable of editing files in Unicode UTF-8 coding
so it's very usable for example by writing WWW pages.
Bloüek can edit very big files with very long lines.
Thanks to Mateusz Viste for his Unicode fonts.
Bloüek is also usable as a simple image viewer for files
in common graphic formats. It is however not able to
edit the images.

This program is released as free and open source under
GNU/GPL license<SF>
