#form_konc_rad
Line ending format

#form_konc_help
I recommend keeping the standard CRLF which is common in 
DOS or Windows systems.
LF is standard for Unix/Linux and
CR is reportedly used in the Macintosh computers.

#form_konc_mozn
CRLF (DOS/win)
LF (Unix)
CR (Mac)

#b_ord_mark
Byte order mark (BOM)

#bom_help
"BOM" = "byte order mark"
It only applies to files in Unicode.
It is two-bytes or three-bytes sequence on the very beginning of the file.
BOM is recommended to use for files in UTF-16.
In UTF-8 documents, it is rarely used.

#bom_mozn
UTF-8
UTF-16le
UTF-16be

